WEBVTT

00:00:02.000 --> 00:00:06.840
In the kitchen of a lawn bowls club, a laminated card is taped to a cupboard door.

00:00:07.140 --> 00:00:07.820
It says:

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:09.260
big urn out of service,

00:00:09.460 --> 00:00:11.210
please use the small one for now.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.540
Tove Ilesanmi first photographed it in March 2023.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:18.160
In August 2025, it was still there.

00:00:18.960 --> 00:00:23.880
His doctoral thesis for the School of Emergent Priorities asks what becomes of arrangements like this,

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:25.600
and in whose favour they end.

00:00:26.400 --> 00:00:31.890
Every fortnight for eleven months, I photographed every notice on display at nine volunteer-run clubs.

00:00:32.190 --> 00:00:35.020
Four hundred and eighteen marked something as temporary.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:38.170
Two-thirds of those named no end-point at all,

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:39.960
just like the card on the cupboard door.

00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:44.530
He then followed two hundred and sixty-nine arrangements, every month for nineteen months.

00:00:45.330 --> 00:00:51.130
Where the notice named an end-point, arrangements were confirmed as permanent more than twice as fast.

00:00:51.430 --> 00:00:53.340
Their rate of reversal was unchanged.

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:58.877
I asked thirty-four members and office-holders what happens when a notice's date comes around.

00:00:58.877 --> 00:01:02.174
Most said it puts the item on a committee agenda.

00:01:02.174 --> 00:01:04.310
None read it as a deadline.

00:01:04.510 --> 00:01:07.590
Sixty-three arrangements reached the meeting their notice had named.

00:01:07.790 --> 00:01:09.750
Fifty-one were confirmed at that meeting,

00:01:09.950 --> 00:01:11.630
and four were reversed.

00:01:12.630 --> 00:01:17.710
The thesis recommends a published register of every pilot, trial and interim measure at the University.

00:01:18.010 --> 00:01:22.660
An entry still unresolved at its review date is confirmed as permanent automatically,

00:01:22.860 --> 00:01:23.960
with no override.

00:01:24.760 --> 00:01:26.386
The date produces the meeting,

00:01:26.586 --> 00:01:29.976
and the meeting, on the material before it, produces the confirmation.
